      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Fri Nov 12 2021 19:38:12 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<div><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">Key benefits</span></span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<ul>\n<li>The Tornier Perform Reversed Augmented Glenoid features four augmented baseplates (25 mm Half-Wedge orFull-Wedge, and 29 mm Half-Wedge or Full-Wedge).&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\n</li>\n<li>The wedged portion of the baseplates utilize Stryker's Adaptis Integrated Porous Metal and was designed to encourage bone ingrowth and may assist in fixation strength.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\n</li>\n<li>These baseplates can be used to help correct glenoid defects in glenoid classifications suggested by Walch et al. and Sirveaux et al.<sup>1, 2</sup></li>\n</ul>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Nov 30 2021 20:10:25 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
